prompt:
Use Three.js CSS3DRenderer to implement an interactive 3D periodic table that supports switching among four layout modes with animated transitions.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { CSS3DRenderer, CSS3DObject } from 'three/addons/renderers/CSS3DRenderer.js';
import { TrackballControls } from 'three/addons/controls/TrackballControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Element Data]
(1) Embed a complete data array containing all 118 chemical elements. Each element must include at least: atomic number (Z), symbol (symbol), name (name), atomic mass (mass), and category (category);
(2) Categories must include at least these 6 categories: alkali-metal, alkaline-earth, transition-metal, post-transition-metal, metalloid, nonmetal, noble-gas, lanthanide, actinide;
(3) Each category must have a corresponding color code, such as alkali-metal=#FF6666 and noble-gas=#FFCC00, and card background colors must be assigned according to category;

[CSS3DObject Cards]
(4) Create one div element for each element, approximately 120×160px in size, containing: the atomic number in the upper-left corner in small text, the element symbol centered in large 36px bold text, the element name below the symbol in 14px text, and the atomic mass at the bottom in 12px text;
(5) Cards must have a semi-transparent rgba background, a 1px solid white/light-colored border, and a 4px border radius;
(6) Wrap each div in a CSS3DObject and add it to the scene;

[Four Layout Modes]
(7) Provide a layout selection control with id="layoutMode", implemented as a select dropdown or button group, with these options: table, helix, sphere, grid;
(8) table layout: arrange the elements in the standard periodic table format with 18 columns and 7 rows, plus two separate rows for the lanthanides and actinides. Map each element's periodic-table row and column position to x and y coordinates in 3D space, with z=0;
(9) helix layout: arrange all 118 elements along a helix using the parametric curve x=900*sin(θ), y=-θ*8+450, z=900*cos(θ), with θ uniformly distributed from 0 to approximately 12π;
(10) sphere layout: distribute all 118 elements uniformly over the surface of a sphere with radius 800, using a Fibonacci sphere distribution or uniform spherical-coordinate sampling. Each card must lookAt the sphere center;
(11) grid layout: arrange all 118 elements in a planar grid with 12 columns, spacing positions by 170×200, with z=0 and the rows and columns centered;

[Animated Transitions]
(12) When switching layouts, smoothly transition all 118 CSS3DObjects from their current positions/rotations to their target positions/rotations. The animation duration must be 1000ms and must use an easing function such as easeInOutCubic;
(13) You may use TWEEN.js, which must either be inlined manually or loaded from this CDN:
https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@tweenjs/tween.js@18.6.4/dist/tween.umd.js
Alternatively, you may implement lerp interpolation manually;
(14) The camera must remain freely rotatable during transitions, and TrackballControls must remain unaffected;

[Element Interaction]
(15) Clicking any element card must open a detailed information panel with id="elementInfo", displaying the atomic number, symbol, name, mass, category, and the total number of elements in that category;
(16) The panel must be a fixed-position DOM overlay with a close button;
(17) Clicking the currently selected element again or clicking the close button must hide the panel;

[Search Filtering]
(18) Provide a text search input with id="searchInput" that supports real-time filtering by element name or symbol;
(19) Matching element cards must remain normally visible, while nonmatching cards must have their opacity reduced to 0.1;
(20) Clearing the search input must restore all cards to full opacity;
(21) Search matching must be case-insensitive;

[Camera and Controls]
(22) CSS3DRenderer must render full-screen;
(23) TrackballControls or a similar controller must provide rotation, zooming, and panning;
(24) Use a dark background color, such as #000511 or a similar deep blue-black color;

[State Exposure (Required)]
(25) Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame with the following fields:
  - elementCount: number (the number of CSS3DObjects in the scene; it should be 118)
  - layout: string (the current layout mode: 'table'|'helix'|'sphere'|'grid')
  - selectedElement: string|null (the symbol of the currently selected element, or null when no element is selected)
  - filteredCount: number (the number of elements currently visible/not filtered out)
  - categoryCount: { alkaliMetal: number, alkalineEarth: number, transitionMetal: number, postTransitionMetal: number, metalloid: number, nonmetal: number, nobleGas: number, lanthanide: number, actinide: number }

Output a single HTML file that can run when opened directly in a browser.
